{title: O Worship the King}
{artist: Robert Grant}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune LYONS - attr. Johann Michael Haydn, in Gardiner's Sacred Melodies (1815)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1833, tune 1815: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [G]worship the King, all [C]glorious a[G]bove,
O [G]gratefully sing His [D]power and His [G]love;
Our [G]Shield and De[D]fender, the [G]Ancient of [D]Days,
Pa[G]vilioned in [C]splendor, and [G]girded [D]with [G]praise.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O [G]tell of His might, O [C]sing of His [G]grace,
Whose [G]robe is the light, whose [D]canopy [G]space,
His [G]chariots of [D]wrath the deep [G]thunderclouds [D]form,
And [G]dark is His [C]path on the [G]wings of [D]the [G]storm.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Frail [G]children of dust, and [C]feeble as [G]frail,
In [G]Thee do we trust, nor [D]find Thee to [G]fail;
Thy [G]mercies how [D]tender, how [G]firm to the [D]end,
Our [G]Maker, De[C]fender, Re[G]deemer, [D]and [G]Friend.
{end_of_verse}
